{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Audio Transformers \u2014 Whisper Architecture Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "See `code/main.py`. We don't train Whisper \u2014 we build the log-mel spectrogram pipeline + task-token prompt formatter. Those are the parts you actually touch in production."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: synthesize audio"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Generate a 1-second sine wave at 440 Hz sampled at 16 kHz. 16,000 samples."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: log-mel spectrogram (simplified)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Full mel spectrogram needs FFT. We do a simplified framing + per-frame energy version that shows the pipeline without requiring `librosa`:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def frame_signal(x, frame_size=400, hop=160):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    frames = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for start in range(0, len(x) - frame_size + 1, hop):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        frames.append(x[start:start + frame_size])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return frames"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Frame = 25 ms, hop = 10 ms. Matches Whisper's windowing. Per-frame energy stands in for mel bins for pedagogy."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: pad to 30 s"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Whisper always processes 30-second chunks. Pad (or clip) the spectrogram to 3,000 frames."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: build the prompt tokens"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def whisper_prompt(lang=\"en\", task=\"transcribe\", timestamps=True):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    tokens = [\"<|startoftranscript|>\", f\"<|{lang}|>\", f\"<|{task}|>\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if not timestamps:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        tokens.append(\"<|notimestamps|>\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return tokens"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "That is the whole task-control surface. A 4-token prefix."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Run `code/main.py`. Confirm the frame count for a 1-second signal at 16 kHz with 10 ms hop is ~100 frames. For 30 seconds: ~3,000 frames.\n2. **Medium.** Build the full log-mel spectrogram using `numpy.fft`. Verify 80 mel bins match `librosa.feature.melspectrogram(n_mels=80)` within numerical error.\n3. **Hard.** Implement streaming inference: chunk audio into 10 s windows with 2 s overlap, run Whisper on each chunk, merge transcripts. Measure word-error rate vs single-pass on a 5-minute podcast sample."
      ]
    }
  ],
